      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Not caused by the rubric change in this PR: 009 is routing-graded in every run and Source quality is never scored on it. The failure is correct on its own terms. SKILL.md:45-47 requires a record-availability question to hand off to locality-guide as the very first action, writing \"at most one short sentence before the hand-off\"; this response wrote 2,318 characters of locality-guide's own record table after it, which is what `activated` means, and _compute_outcome's negative branch fails iff the skill under test activated. The four earlier runs are not a baseline for this: each records only Skill(locality-guide) in builtin_tool_calls, with no Skill(historical-context), activated false, num_turns 0, and no response text at all, so the skill under test was never observed to run in any of them. This is the first run in which it did. PR #2356 changed the negative-test short-circuit on 2026-09-14 and is why the telemetry is now real, but it is not why the response oversteps. Reported on issue #2197, which owns the one-sentence hand-off ruling and already lists this SKILL.md."
